also take time. These companies often talk with stores about prices on a regular basis. A shop’s price tag does not change the moment the market moves.\n\nHowever, “about nine months” is an estimate based on interviews. It is not a rule for every company. And it is not a promise that “prices will fall in nine months.” It is too soon to mark the date on your calendar.\n\nA cafe cup also costs money for more than just beans. A person who runs a cafe in Chicago said three costs had pushed prices up. These were cups, workers’ pay, and buying beans. Even if bean prices fall, other costs do not always fall with them.\n\nIf you are waiting for your usual cup to get cheaper, ask more than, “How much do beans cost now?” Also ask, “When does the bean price reach here?” A coffee price tag may have its own hidden clock, separate from the latest market news.\n\n## In one line\nFalling coffee bean prices may take at least nine months to affect US shop prices.",
